# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values you actually use.
# .env is gitignored — never commit real credentials.

# --- Optional cloud backup (api/state.js) ---
# Free Upstash Redis database. Two ways to get these two values:
#
#   1. Reuse the same free Upstash database D:\ReactApp\ledger-app already
#      runs on (its server/services/storage.kv.js uses the exact same
#      UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL/TOKEN pair). Safe to share: it's plain
#      key-value storage with no schema, and fire-dashboard's data lives
#      entirely under its own "fire-dashboard:" key prefix, with zero
#      overlap with ledger-app's "config:"/"txn:"/"u:{userId}:" keys. Both
#      apps then share the same free-tier quota (500K commands/month,
#      256MB) — fine for two personal apps, but worth knowing. Copy the two
#      values straight from ledger-app's own .env file.
#   2. Or provision a separate one: via the Vercel Marketplace
#      (`vercel install upstash`, or Vercel dashboard → Storage → Add →
#      Upstash) or directly at https://upstash.com (free tier, no card
#      required — adding a card switches the account to pay-as-you-go).
#
# On Vercel, installing the integration injects these automatically; either
# way you only need to set them here for local dev. Leave both unset and the
# app works exactly as before (localStorage-only) — the "Cloud sync" card in
# the Snapshots tab just shows "not configured".
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# --- Optional: pin a specific Python interpreter for local CAS import ---
# Only needed if server.js's automatic py/python/python3 detection picks the
# wrong one. Full path to a real python.exe (not the Microsoft Store stub).
# CAS_PYTHON_BIN=
